  partName: Oil Pump
  description: The oil pump is a small, thin-flat component positioned on the left
    side of the engine, responsible for circulating oil throughout the engine and
    maintaining lubrication. Its metal-mid material and moderate vertex count indicate
    a focus on durability and flow management. The oil pump is a critical component
    of the engine, requiring precise design and engineering to achieve reliable operation
    and prevent oil starvation.
